 - **Day periods and colouring** — night, morning, day and evening follow the sun at each location. Day tracks and hour cells are coloured plainly, by time of day or by your working hours. ([day-periods](openspec/specs/day-periods/spec.md), [day-colouring](openspec/specs/day-colouring/spec.md))
 - **Grid view and meeting ranges** — pick a meeting range at any minute, see it in every location's local time and share it as text with Share meeting, which opens a dialog to pick the locations, the language and the zone label. ([grid-view](openspec/specs/grid-view/spec.md), [meeting-range](openspec/specs/meeting-range/spec.md), [meeting-share-dialog](openspec/specs/meeting-share-dialog/spec.md))
 - **Settings** — theme, hour format (12 or 24), view, day colouring and working hours, zone label parts and interface language. ([settings](openspec/specs/settings/spec.md), [app-shell](openspec/specs/app-shell/spec.md))
-- **Tools** *(in development)* — optional capabilities turned on in the settings, each with its own button in the header. The first one is the Unix time converter: paste a Unix time or an ISO 8601 text and read the exact time in every location. ([tools](openspec/specs/tools/spec.md), [unix-time-converter](openspec/specs/unix-time-converter/spec.md))
+- **Tools** — optional capabilities turned on in the settings, each with its own button in the header. The first one is the Unix time converter: paste a Unix time or an ISO 8601 text and read the exact time in every location. ([tools](openspec/specs/tools/spec.md), [unix-time-converter](openspec/specs/unix-time-converter/spec.md))
 - **Offline work and updates** — installable PWA that works offline; a new app version shows an update notice with Reload (the app never reloads by itself), while data-only builds (zone rules, city data) update silently; a zone rules update notice appears only when a new release changes a zone you watch. ([app-delivery](openspec/specs/app-delivery/spec.md), [zone-rules-updates](openspec/specs/zone-rules-updates/spec.md))
 - **Data and engines** — the app compiles its own IANA zone rules, uses GeoNames city data and runs on legacy iOS Safari. ([zone-rules](openspec/specs/zone-rules/spec.md), [city-data](openspec/specs/city-data/spec.md), [browser-compatibility](openspec/specs/browser-compatibility/spec.md))
 
